{"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V5indexyyxmSHRzAA9ComponentRzlF","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"index"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type)"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ValueIndex.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/ValueIndex.swift#L243"},"title":"index(_:)","extendedModule":"WorldModule","symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"mutating"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"index"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"type"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule9ComponentP","text":"Component"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"type","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The component type to index.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use an index when you often look entities up by a component’s value, such as finding an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity by its name:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let bob = world.spawn(Name(value: \"bob\"), Health(current: 3))","world.spawn(Name(value: \"ada\"), Health(current: 4))","world.index(Name.self)","","print(world.lookup(Name(value: \"bob\")) == [bob])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Spawning, inserting, removing and despawning keep the index current. A change made in place,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the world’s subscript, an update or a mutable span, leaves the index out of date"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until the next "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/advanceChangeTick()"},{"type":"text","text":", which a schedule calls before each system, rebuilds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it. Until then, "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" walks the storage, so its answer is always current. Index a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type whose values change rarely. Indexing a type twice keeps one index. A copy of the world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps its indexes; a snapshot doesn’t."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" entities holding a ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],